{
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Here's the plan for the hinged box. Steps 1 to 4 are design work and need no approval. Printing (steps 5 and 6) only happens if you ask for it.\n\n1. Plan the box: base, lid, and a 3 mm pin hinge along the back edge.\n2. Confirm the sizes on a dimension sheet.\n3. Build the base, the lid, and the hinge knuckles and pin.\n4. Check the part against the plan and the print-in-place gaps.\n5. Slice on your P1S (PLA, 0.4 nozzle) when you ask.\n6. Send to the printer, which needs your OK.",
      "calls": [
        {
          "name": "design.plan",
          "args": {
            "part": "Hinged box with lid",
            "units": "mm",
            "features": [
              {
                "name": "Base shell",
                "kind": "extrude",
                "sizes": {
                  "length": 80,
                  "width": 50,
                  "height": 25,
                  "wall": 2
                }
              },
              {
                "name": "Lid shell",
                "kind": "extrude",
                "sizes": {
                  "length": 80,
                  "width": 50,
                  "height": 10,
                  "wall": 2
                }
              },
              {
                "name": "Hinge knuckles",
                "kind": "extrude",
                "sizes": {
                  "knuckle_outer_diameter": 7,
                  "gap": 0.4
                }
              },
              {
                "name": "Hinge pin",
                "kind": "extrude",
                "sizes": {
                  "pin_diameter": 3
                }
              }
            ],
            "assumptions": [
              "Overall closed size is 80 x 50 x 35 mm: base 25 mm tall plus lid 10 mm tall.",
              "Walls are 2 mm on the base and lid.",
              "Pin hinge runs along the full back edge (the 80 mm side), with the pin as a separate rod through the knuckles.",
              "Pin diameter 3 mm and knuckle outer diameter 7 mm are guesses, not from a source.",
              "Print-in-place gap of 0.4 mm suits PLA on a 0.4 mm nozzle."
            ],
            "questions": [
              "Should the lid be closed on top, or open with a lip that sits inside the base?",
              "Do you want the pin to print as part of the assembly, or as a separate piece?"
            ],
            "printInPlace": [
              "Base shell",
              "Lid shell"
            ],
            "reason": "Pin hinge along the back edge, print-in-place lid and base."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
