    },
    {
      "text": "The box is partly built, but the hinge is not finished, so the part is not done.\n\n**What's in the design:** the base is an 80 x 50 x 25 mm tray with 2 mm walls, and the lid is an 80 x 50 x 10 mm tray with 2 mm walls, laid beside it on the bed. The hinge knuckles and a 3 mm pin are there too. The sizes you confirmed are in the plan, and the pin, knuckle, and 0.4 mm gap sizes are my guesses.\n\n**What fails:** the hinge is fused solid, so the lid cannot swing. The base, the knuckles, the pin, and the lid all touch at zero gap, and the plan needs at least 0.3 mm side by side and 0.4 mm above or below between moving pieces. My first build fused the hinge pieces together instead of separating them, and I used the one fix round on the check without fixing it. I stopped there rather than try again blind.\n\n**Next step:** I can rebuild just the hinge so the knuckles belong to each half, with a 0.4 mm clearance between the lid and base knuckles and the pin running through the bore. Should I rebuild it that way, or would you rather print the lid and base as two separate pieces with no pin?"
    }
  ]
